  "subnode": "INP-02",
  "trigger_name": "Voluntary / Third-Party Report",
  "summary_html": "Any person (not just mandated reporters) may submit a **voluntary report** to child-protection authorities. CAPTA requires states to maintain mechanisms for intake, confidentiality, and immunity policies tied to federal funding. In Wyoming the report is not optional: any person who knows or has reasonable cause to believe or suspect that a child has been abused or neglected must report it immediately (Wyo. Stat. § 14-3-205(a)).",
  "authority_html": "- **CAPTA (42 U.S.C. §§ 5101–5116)** — requires states to operate intake/report systems that accept voluntary reports and protect good-faith reporters",
  "icon": "🗣️",
